hadiths[46]{hadithnumber,text}:
"8","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Islam is built upon five (pillars): (1) Bearing witness that there is no deity except Allah and bearing witness that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, (2) establishing prayer, (3) giving zakat, (4) performing Hajj, (5) fasting in Ramadan."
"9","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Faith has over sixty branches, and modesty is one of the branches of faith."
"10","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: “A (true) Muslim is the one from whose tongue and hand (other) Muslims are safe, and (the real) emigrant is the one who abandons what Allah the Exalted has forbidden.”"
"11","Narrated Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him): (On one occasion) the companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! Which Islam is the best?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""(The Islam of) the one from whose tongue and hand (other) Muslims are safe."
"12","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""Which Islam is best?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Feed (others) and greet with Salam those whom you know and those whom you do not know (all of them)."
"13","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""None of you will have faith until he wishes for his brother (Muslim) what he wishes for himself."
"14","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""By Him in Whose Hand is my soul! None of you can be a believer until I become more beloved to him than his father and his children."
"15","A narration similar to this is reported from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him), and in it there is this addition that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""And (I do not become) more beloved than all people."
"16","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""Whoever possesses three qualities will taste the sweetness of faith: (1) Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him) are more beloved to him than anything else; (2) he loves someone only for the sake of Allah; (3) he hates to return to disbelief as much as he would hate to be thrown into the fire."
"17","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Loving the Ansar is a sign of being a believer, and harboring enmity towards the Ansar is a sign of being a hypocrite."
"18","Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""While a group of the noble Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) was sitting around him, he said: 'Pledge allegiance to me on the condition that you will not associate anything with Allah, and you will not steal, and you will not commit adultery, and you will not kill your children, and you will not slander anyone by fabricating a falsehood which you invent between your hands and feet (i.e., deliberately), and you will not disobey (Allah and His Messenger) in any good matter. Whoever among you fulfills this pledge, his reward is with Allah. And whoever falls into any of these (evil) matters and is punished for it in this world, then that punishment will be an expiation for him. And whoever falls into any of these (evil) matters and Allah conceals it for him (in this world), then his case is with Allah: if He wills, He will pardon him, and if He wills, He will punish him.' (Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him) says:) We all pledged allegiance to him (peace and blessings be upon him) on these matters."
"19","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah said: ""There will soon come a time when the best wealth of a Muslim will be sheep which he will take to the tops of mountains and places of rainfall, fleeing with his religion from tribulations."
"20","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would command people (to do good deeds), he would command them to do such deeds that they could (always) perform (he never encouraged them to perform burdensome acts of worship). (Once) the noble companions (may Allah be pleased with them) submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! We are not like you. Surely Allah has forgiven all your past and future sins (therefore, we should worship more than you)."" Upon this, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) became angry until the effect of anger appeared on his (blessed) face. Then he said: ""I am the one among you who knows Allah the most and fears Him the most."
"21","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he (peace be upon him) said: ""(When) the people of Paradise will have entered Paradise and the people of Hell will have entered Hell, then after that Allah Almighty will say (to the angels): 'Whoever has in his heart even a mustard seed's weight of faith, take him out (from Hell).' So they will be taken out from Hell, and they will have become blackened (by burning). Then they will be thrown into the stream of Hayat (rain) or the stream of Life."" These words of doubt are from Imam Malik (who is one of the narrators of the hadith). ""Then they will become fresh as a seed grows fresh in the flow of water. (O person!) Have you not seen that it comes out yellow and intertwined?"
"22","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""While I was sleeping, I saw (in a dream) that people were being presented before me and they were wearing shirts. Some shirts reached only up to their chests, and some were even shorter, and 'Umar bin Al-Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) was also presented before me, and the shirt he was wearing was so long that he was dragging it (as he walked)."" The Companions (may Allah be pleased with them) asked, ""O Messenger of Allah! How did you interpret it?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""(The shirt) means religion."
"23","Narrated Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) once passed by an Ansari man who was advising his brother regarding modesty. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""Leave him (from advising about modesty), for modesty is a part of faith."
"24","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""I have been commanded to fight the people until they testify that there is no deity except Allah and that Muhammad (peace be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah, and establish prayer and give zakat. So when they do this, they will have protected their blood and their wealth from me except by the right of Islam, and their reckoning is with Allah."
"25","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked: ""Which deed is the best?"" He (peace be upon him) replied: ""To have faith in Allah and His Messenger (peace be upon him)."" Then he was asked: ""Which deed is best after that?"" He said: ""Jihad in the way of Allah."" Then he was asked: ""Which deed is best after that?"" He replied: ""A Hajj that is accepted (by Allah)."
"26","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave (wealth) to some people while Sa’d (may Allah be pleased with him) was sitting there. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left out a person (i.e., did not give him) who seemed to me the best among them, so I said, “O Messenger of Allah! What is the reason that you ignored such-and-such person? By Allah, I consider him a believer.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “(You consider him) a believer or a Muslim?” I remained silent for a while, then what I knew about that person compelled me, so I repeated my statement, that is, I said, “What is the reason that you ignored such-and-such person? By Allah, I consider him a believer.” The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “(You consider him) a believer or a Muslim?” Then I remained silent for a while. After that, what I knew about that person compelled me, so I repeated my statement again, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) also gave the same reply again. Finally, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, “O Sa’d! Sometimes I give to a person out of fear that (if he is not given, he might become a disbeliever and) Allah may throw him headlong into the Fire, even though another person is dearer to me than him. (I do not give to the latter because I do not have such a concern about him).”"
"27","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Prophet Muhammad (peace be upon him) said: “(Once) Hell was shown to me and I saw that the majority of its inhabitants were women. The reason is that they commit disbelief.” It was asked, “Do they disbelieve in Allah?” He (peace be upon him) replied: “They are ungrateful to their husbands and do not acknowledge favors. (It happens) that if you do good to a woman for a long time and then she sees something (displeasing) from you, she will immediately say, ‘I have never received any good from you.’”"
"28","Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I abused a person (who was my slave), that is, I taunted him about his mother. (This news) reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: ""O Abu Dharr! Did you taunt him about his mother? Indeed, you are a person in whom there is still some (remnant) of ignorance (jahiliyyah). Your slaves are your brothers. Allah has placed them under your authority. So, whoever has his brother under his authority, he should feed him what he himself eats and clothe him with what he himself wears, and (listen) do not make them do work that is too difficult for them, and if you do assign them such a task, then help them with it yourself."
"29","Narrated Abu Bakrah (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When two Muslims meet each other with their swords (i.e., fight), both the killer and the one killed are in Hellfire."" I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! (It is understandable) for the killer, but what about the one who is killed?"" He (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""(It is because) he was eager to kill his companion."
"30","Narrated by Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): ""When this verse was revealed: 'Those who believe and do not mix their belief with injustice...' (Al-An'am: 82), the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) became very worried and said, 'Who among us has not committed injustice?' So Allah, the Most Great and Exalted, revealed this verse: 'Indeed, associating partners with Allah is a great injustice.' (Luqman: 13)."
"31","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""There are three characteristics of a hypocrite: (1) When he speaks, he lies; (2) When he makes a promise, he breaks it; (3) When something is entrusted to him, he betrays the trust."
"32","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Whoever possesses four traits is a pure hypocrite, and whoever has one of these four traits has a trait of hypocrisy until he gives it up. (These four traits are:) (1) When entrusted, he betrays the trust; (2) When he speaks, he lies; (3) When he makes a promise, he breaks it; (4) When he quarrels, he behaves in an obscene manner.”"
"33","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands (in prayer) in the Night of Qadr out of faith and seeking reward, all his past sins will be forgiven."
"34","Narrated Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Allah guarantees for the person who goes out in His path (for jihad), and nothing drove him out except faith in Allah and belief in His messengers, that either I (i.e., Allah) will return him with the reward and (war) booty that he obtained in jihad, or I will admit him into Paradise (as a martyr). And (the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said) if I did not find it hard for my ummah, I would never stay behind from any expedition (i.e., a battle in which the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, did not participate), and I (i.e., the Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him) certainly love that I be killed in the path of Allah, then brought back to life, then killed again, then brought back to life, then killed again."
"35","Narrated from Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever stands (in prayer) in Ramadan, with faith and seeking reward, all his past sins will be forgiven."
"36","Narrated by Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever fasts during the month of Ramadan out of faith and seeking reward, all his past sins will be forgiven."
"37","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Religion is very easy, and whoever makes religion hard upon himself will be overpowered by it. (As a result, he will not be able to bear the self-imposed hardship.) So, adopt the right and moderate way, and remain close (to one another), and rejoice (that you have been given such an easy religion), and gain strength by worshipping in the morning, after noon, and for a while at night."
"38","Narrated from Sayyiduna Bara bin Azib (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) migrated to Madinah, he first stayed with his maternal or paternal relatives who were from the Ansar. After arriving in Madinah, the Prophet (peace be upon him) prayed facing Bayt al-Maqdis for sixteen or seventeen months, but he preferred that his Qiblah be towards the Ka'bah (and so it happened). The very first prayer that the Prophet (peace be upon him) offered facing the Ka'bah was the 'Asr prayer, and some people joined him in that prayer. One of them left and passed by a mosque where he saw people praying facing Bayt al-Maqdis, so he said, ""I bear witness before Allah that I have prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him) facing Makkah."" (Upon hearing this) those people turned towards the Ka'bah in the same state they were in. When the Prophet (peace be upon him) used to pray facing Bayt al-Maqdis, the Jews and all the People of the Book were very pleased, but when the Prophet (peace be upon him) turned his face towards the Ka'bah, it was very displeasing to them."
"39","Narrated Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: When a person becomes a Muslim and his Islam becomes good (excellent and strong), Allah Almighty forgives all the sins he had committed before. After that, the reckoning begins: a good deed is rewarded from ten times up to seven hundred times, and a bad deed is recorded as it is, unless Allah Almighty pardons it."
"40","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that (once) the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to her and (saw that) there was a woman (sitting) with her. The Prophet (peace be upon him) asked: “Who is this?” Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) replied that this is such-and-such woman (and) began to mention the abundance of her prayers. So the Prophet (peace be upon him) said: “Stop (look), take upon yourselves only as much (acts) as you are able to do (consistently), for Allah does not tire (of giving reward) until you tire (of worship), and the most beloved deed to Allah is that which is done regularly by its doer.”"
"41","Narrated by Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: ""Whoever says 'La ilaha illallah' and in his heart there is goodness (i.e., faith) equal to a grain of barley, he will come out of Hell. Whoever says 'La ilaha illallah' and in his heart there is goodness (i.e., faith) equal to a grain of wheat, he will come out of Hell. And whoever says 'La ilaha illallah' and in his heart there is goodness (i.e., faith) equal to the smallest particle, he will come out of Hell."
"42","It is narrated from Amir al-Mu'minin Umar bin Khattab (may Allah be pleased with him) that a Jew said to him, ""O Amir al-Mu'minin! There is an ayah in your Book (i.e., the Qur'an) which you recite. If it had been revealed to us, that is, to the Jews, we would have taken the day (on which it was revealed) as a festival."" Amir al-Mu'minin asked, ""Which ayah is that?"" The Jew replied, ""This ayah: 'Today I (Allah) have perfected your religion for you, completed My favor upon you, and have chosen for you Islam as your religion.' (Al-Ma'idah: 3)"" Upon hearing this, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Indeed, we remember the day and the place in which this ayah was revealed to the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace be upon him) was standing in 'Arafah on that day, and it was a Friday."
"43","Narrated from Sayyiduna Talhah bin Ubaidullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that a man from Najd, disheveled in appearance, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). We could hear the humming of his voice but could not understand what he was saying. When he came closer, (we found out that) he was asking the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) about Islam. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: There are five prayers in the day and night. The man asked: Is there any prayer obligatory upon me other than these? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, except if you do something voluntarily (nafl). (Then) the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: And fasting in the month of Ramadan. He asked: Is there any other fasting obligatory upon me besides this? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, except if you do it voluntarily. (Sayyiduna Talhah, may Allah be pleased with him, says) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also mentioned zakat to him. He asked: Is there any charity obligatory upon me other than this? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: No, except if you give voluntarily. Sayyiduna Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that then the man turned away saying: By Allah! I will neither add to these (mentioned obligations) nor decrease from them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If he is speaking the truth, he will be successful."
"44","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever follows the funeral of a Muslim out of faith and seeking reward, and remains with it until the funeral prayer is offered and the burial is completed, he returns with two qirats of reward, and each qirat is like (the mountain of) Uhud. And whoever offers the funeral prayer and returns before the burial, he returns with one qirat of reward."
"45","Narrated by Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him): The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abusing a Muslim is wickedness and fighting him is disbelief."
"46","Narrated Sayyiduna Ubadah bin Samit (may Allah be pleased with him): The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out (once) to inform the people about the (exact) Night of Qadr, but (coincidentally at that time) two Muslims were fighting with each other. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came out to inform you about the (exact) Night of Qadr, but since so-and-so and so-and-so were fighting, (the definite knowledge of it) was taken away (from the world), and perhaps this is better for you. (Now) seek the Night of Qadr in the twenty-seventh, twenty-ninth, and twenty-fifth (nights) of Ramadan."
"47","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` one day the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was sitting before the people when suddenly a man came before him and asked (him), ""What is faith?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Faith is that you believe in Allah, and in His angels, and in His books, and in (the Hereafter) meeting Allah, and in Allah's messengers, and you have certainty in the Day of Judgment."" (Then) that man asked, ""What is Islam?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Islam is that you worship Allah and do not associate anything with Him, and you establish prayer, and pay the obligatory zakat, and fast in Ramadan."" (Then) that man asked, ""What is Ihsan?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: ""Ihsan is that you worship Allah (with such humility, devotion, and sincerity) as if you are seeing Him, and if you do not achieve this state that you see Him, then (at least) know that He surely sees you."" Then that man asked, ""When will the Hour (Day of Judgment) be?"" In reply, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The one being asked does not know more about it than the questioner (rather, both are equally unaware)."" ""However, I will tell you its signs: (1) When a slave woman gives birth to her master, and (2) when the barefooted, naked, destitute shepherds compete in constructing tall buildings, then know that the Hour is near. And the knowledge of the Hour is among those five things which none knows except Allah."" Then the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited the entire verse: ""Indeed, with Allah alone is the knowledge of the Hour..."" (Luqman: 34). After that, the man left, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said (to the noble Companions, may Allah be pleased with them): ""Bring him back to me."" (So the people went to bring him back) but found no one there. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""That was Jibreel (Gabriel, peace be upon him); he came to teach the people their religion."
"48","Narrated Nu'man bin Bashir (may Allah be pleased with him): I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""The lawful is clear and the unlawful is (also) clear, and between them are doubtful matters which many people do not know. So whoever avoids the doubtful matters has protected his religion and his honor, and whoever falls into doubtful matters is like a shepherd who grazes (his animals) near a sanctuary; it is likely that he will soon enter it. Beware! Every king has a sanctuary, and beware! The sanctuary of Allah on His earth is His prohibited things. Beware! There is a piece of flesh in the body; if it is sound, the whole body is sound, and if it is corrupt, the whole body is corrupt. Beware! That piece is the heart."
"49","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both): When the people of ‘Abdul Qais (the tribe of ‘Abdul Qais) came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said to them: “Which people are you, or (he asked) which delegation are you?” They replied, “(We are) from the family of Rabi‘ah.” He said, “Welcome to the people or the delegation! You will neither be disgraced nor regretful.” Then they said, “O Messenger of Allah! We cannot come to you except in the sacred months, for between us and you is the tribe of Mudar (who are disbelievers), and we fear them. So, please tell us something clear (a summary of rulings) that we may inform those we left behind, and by which we may enter Paradise.” They also asked him about drinks (which are lawful and which are unlawful). So, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded them with four things and forbade them from four things. (1) He commanded them to believe in Allah alone, and said: “Do you know what it means to believe in Allah alone?” They replied, “Allah and His Messenger know best.” He said: “It is to testify that there is no god (worthy of worship) except Allah, and that Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the Messenger of Allah; to establish prayer; to give zakat; to fast in Ramadan; and to give one-fifth of the war booty (to the treasury).” And he forbade them from four things (i.e., from drinking from four types of vessels): (1) From green glazed jars, (2) From gourds, (3) From hollowed-out wooden vessels, (4) From oil jars. And sometimes (Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, would say) “muqayyar” instead of “muzaffat.” And the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Remember these things and convey them to those you left behind.”"
"50","Narrated from Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Actions (are judged) according to intentions, and this hadith has already been mentioned (see the Book: The Beginning of the Revelation to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)... Chapter: How the Revelation Began to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)...), and (here) there is an addition that (the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said): And for every person is what he intended. Therefore, whoever's migration is for Allah and His Messenger, then (with Allah) his migration is for that (purpose) for which he migrated."
"51","`Sayyiduna Abu Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that` he (peace be upon him) said: When a man spends on his family considering it as a rewardable act, it is counted as charity for him."
"52","`Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah Bajali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I pledged allegiance to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on establishing prayer, giving zakat, and wishing well for every Muslim."
"53","Narrated from Sayyiduna Jarir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him): I presented myself before the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and said that I wish to pledge allegiance to you on Islam. So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) stipulated for me to remain steadfast on Islam and to wish well for every Muslim. Thus, I pledged allegiance to him on this."
